<h1>What to craft next in MTG Arena, Mardu colors (white, black, red)</h1>
<p class="sub">Standard format, June 2026. This page reads your live Magic: The Gathering Arena collection and ranks every card you might want to make using a Wildcard. The cards that show up in the most decks rise to the top.</p>

<div class="note">
<strong>One-paragraph explainer.</strong> In MTG Arena you turn extra cards into "Wildcards", then spend a Wildcard to make any card of that rarity. Wildcards are the most precious thing in the game. This dashboard sorts every white, black, or red Standard card by how many of the 17 currently-popular decks in those colors can include it. The more decks a card fits into, the more value you get per Wildcard. You have <strong>12 rare and 8 mythic Wildcards</strong> right now, so the ranking matters.
</div>


<div class="auditbox">
  <h3>Fact audit, 2026-07-18</h3>
  <p style="margin:0 0 8px">Every card claim on this page was re-checked against live Scryfall.</p>
  <ul style="margin:0 0 8px 18px">
    <li><span class="good">20 of 20</span> ranked cards verified: name, rarity, and colour identity all match, and every one is Standard-legal.</li>
    <li><span class="good">4 of 4</span> ban claims confirmed: Cori-Steel Cutter, Heartfire Hero, Monstrous Rage, and Screaming Nemesis all return <code>banned</code> in Standard.</li>
    <li><span class="bad">1 error corrected:</span> the collection total read <code>10,735</code> and the export says <code>11,235</code>, a difference of +225. Fixed on this page, and the collection has since been re-pulled to 11,235 on 2026-07-30.</li>
    <li><span class="good">Snapshot is current:</span> the collection is stamped <b>2026-07-30</b>, with <b>12 rare</b> and <b>8 mythic</b> wildcards. Finishing every 4-of in this pool needs <b>36</b> wildcards, so treat the ranking as a priority order rather than a shopping list.</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin:0"><b>New column: Paper $.</b> Market price for one copy, cheapest Scryfall printing, sortable. Arena charges wildcards rather than dollars, so read it as the paper value of the same card. Priced 76 of 76 rows.</p>
</div>
