<h2 id="filters">Filter and sort the table</h2>
<p class="sub">The table below has 76 rows. <strong>Hide lands</strong> shows only spells. <strong>Hide already at 4-of</strong> shows only cards you still need (a "playset" is 4 copies because that's the deck-building limit). <strong>Hide rotating in early 2027</strong> drops cards from the sets leaving Standard at the next rotation. Correction, 2026-07-18: Standard has NO rotation during 2026. Wizards moved rotation to the first release of each calendar year starting in 2027, so Wilds of Eldraine (WOE) and The Lost Caverns of Ixalan (LCI) stay Standard legal through 2026 and rotate in early 2027, not this fall. An earlier version of this page hid those cards as rotating and would have talked you out of crafting cards that are legal for months yet. All three filters start ON; click a lit button to turn it off. For sorting, use the <strong>Wildcards needed</strong> and <strong>Deck count</strong> buttons, or click any column header. (Win rate is a per-deck number, not a per-card one, so its sort lives down in the 25-deck section below.)</p>
